            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Then I am confused about this PR. If the server returns `plaintext`, then we should treat it as plaintext and not pretend it's Markdown to be stripped of markup.\n\nIf a server returns Markdown as kind `plaintext`, it's broken, plain and simple, and needs to be fixed. Our (very reasonable) policy has always been \"don't add hacks for broken servers\".\n\nConversely, if it _is_ plaintext, why are we adding custom markup to it? We cannot rely _at all_ on the contents of this field for arbitrary servers; \"clangd does this\" is not a good policy...",
            "commit_id": "9dc8afd25d963266ae99955512be8ee0b6993cc0",
