            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "the fences aren't from the server, we add them. detail gets wrapped in ````ft and stuck in front of the docs, so once there's a detail the info is markdown anyway, but info_kind still says plaintext -> literal fences in the popup. happens with any server that sends detail + plaintext docs, not a clangd thing. the ```text wrap is just so the plaintext doesn't get mangled once it's inside markdown (__STDC__ -> bold STDC etc).\r\n\r\n@justinmk no, still plaintext when there's no detail or the detail is already in the docs.\r\n\r\nif you'd rather not touch plaintext docs at all, I can just not fence the detail when docs are plaintext and keep it all plaintext. detail loses highlighting but nothing gets wrapped. either works for me",
            "commit_id": "9dc8afd25d963266ae99955512be8ee0b6993cc0",
